# mole whitelist - paths `mo clean` must never touch on this machine.
#
# Managed by dotfiles (disk-prune/config/mole-whitelist.template) and
# overwritten by disk-prune/install.sh: this file is policy, so edit it in
# the repo, not here. Blank lines and # comments are ignored by mole.

# The Trash is user data. mole would otherwise empty it entirely; instead
# Finder's "Remove items after 30 days" owns it (enabled in the osx script)
# and disk-prune just reports its size.
__HOME__/.Trash

# Chrome's on-device AI models. The disk-prune watch list promises these are
# reported, never pruned; without these lines mole cleans all three whenever
# Chrome is closed (lib/clean/user.sh, "Chrome on-device model cache").
__HOME__/Library/Application Support/Google/Chrome/OptGuideOnDeviceModel
__HOME__/Library/Application Support/Google/Chrome/OptGuideOnDeviceClassifierModel
__HOME__/Library/Application Support/Google/Chrome/optimization_guide_model_store
